AArch64 arm64-release-plainstore
(* Counterfactual, NOT emitted by any shipped variant.
   Once lce becomes the slot-ownership word (the fix), Release must clear tid
   BEFORE lce and the lce clear must carry release ordering. This file shows
   what happens if that clear were a plain STR: the two stores may be observed
   out of order, so a thread that wins the claim CAS and writes its own tid can
   have it wiped by the departing thread's tid clear.
   Violated when the slot is claimed (lce=1) but its tid was erased. *)
{ 0:X0=tid; 0:X1=lce; 1:X0=lce; 1:X1=tid; }
 P0            | P1              ;
 STR WZR,[X0]  | MOV X2,#0       ;
 STR XZR,[X1]  | MOV X3,#1       ;
               | CASAL X2,X3,[X0];
               | MOV W4,#2       ;
               | STR W4,[X1]     ;
exists (lce=1 /\ tid=0)